NOTE ON INTENDED USE

JamfDisabler is a personal-privacy tool for computers you own or are authorised
to administer. It deliberately does not hide itself, does not delete anything
and can be undone with a single command.

Managed machines are usually managed for a reason (security updates, disk
encryption, compliance). Blocking the management agent on a machine that is not
yours, or that your school/employer requires, may break agreements you have with
them. Use it on your own hardware, and prefer talking to your IT department over
bypassing them.
